  "short_answer": "Too little dietary iodine prevents the synthesis of T3 and T4, leading to elevated TSH via negative feedback. The high TSH stimulates the overproduction and accumulation of thyroglobulin and colloid within the thyroid follicles without converting it into thyroid hormone, causing the gland to enlarge into a goiter."
}
